# Datasets. Tens of GB of CSV and Parquet, obtained from the source named in
# DATA_LICENSE.md and never committed.
aml-platform/data/
**/data/bronze/
**/data/silver/
**/data/gold/
*.csv
*.parquet
!aml-platform/tests/fixtures/*.csv

# Environments and caches.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.DS_Store
*.log

# Build output. `build/` once held a stale second copy of io.py, sweep.py and
# train.py that had drifted from src/aml, so a reader or scanner saw two
# apparent implementations of the same module.
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# Coverage. `.coverage` is a SQLite database embedding absolute local paths,
# so a committed copy leaks the maintainer's directory layout and is not a
# portable report.
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# A .gitignore entry is not a privacy control.
#
# `Cloud/_v1_superseded/` was listed here while its five files were already
# tracked from an earlier commit. Ignoring a tracked file does not untrack it,
# so the entry read like a control and was not one.
#
# Anything that must not be published must not be committed in the first
# place. Personal notes that are not part of the project belong in a global
# ignore file (`git config --global core.excludesFile`), not here, where the
# list itself would describe material the repository is meant not to contain.
